# Commands and results

## Registry / schema

- `openspec list --json && openspec validate --all --strict`
  - Result: `Totals: 20 passed, 0 failed (20 items)` - PASS.
- `PYTHONPATH=agent .venv/bin/python scripts/validate-semantic-planning-contract.py`
  - Result: `Semantic planning contract valid: snapshotId=sha256:4f84a33d2c021284ca2b45ed105344cc7506118a3787e445cf4bed61d6c9082e` - PASS.
  - New snapshotId substituted into `evals/matcher_cases.yaml` (14 occurrences).

## Agent test suite

- `PYTHONPATH=agent .venv/bin/python -m pytest agent/tests/ -q`
  - Result: `1139 passed, 1 skipped in 29.36s` - PASS.
  - New tests added: `test_mrp_element_lines_are_preserved_in_availability_fact_evidence`,
    `test_narrate_fact_llm_path_includes_mrp_element_detail`.
  - Updated tests: `test_narration_guidance_inventory` (new guidance wording),
    `test_capability_registry_v2_declares_fact_binding_contract` + `test_plan_graph_matches_published_registry_and_relation_catalog`
    (dedup semantics for two primaryFact outputs sharing one factTypeRef),
    `test_parse_context_candidates_prompt_includes_read_language_hints` (realigned aliases/examples).
  - Updated production code: `_project_produces_fact_types` (`capability_card.py`) now dedups factTypeRef.

## Inventory eval

- `PYTHONPATH=agent .venv/bin/python -m sap_nexus_agent.eval evals/inventory_availability_cases.yaml`
  - Result: `Eval passed: 7/7` - PASS.

## Frontend verify

- `npm --prefix frontend run verify`
  - Result: `523 passed` of 524; 1 failure (`adapter-integration.test.ts` L3 Action approval flow).
  - Confirmed PRE-EXISTING: `git stash` (no-change baseline) reproduces the same single failure; unrelated to this change (WRITE/approval flow, not inventory).

## Java gateway (jco)

- `JAVA_HOME=... /tmp/gradle-8.8/bin/gradle -p services/gateway :jco:test --tests "com.sapnexus.gateway.jco.InventoryAvailabilityExecutorTest" --no-daemon`
  - Result: `BUILD SUCCESSFUL` - PASS.
  - Test extended: asserts `mrpElementLines` array contains all rows (BE + WB), not just the WB scalar.

## Git

- `git status --short` before/after: only intended files touched (see implementation scope).

# Skipped checks

- None for this change scope. Full release gate (`npm --prefix frontend run release-gate`) not run: it is the workstream-level gate, not required for a single-capability change (per CLAUDE.md §4 "run only what the change touches").

# Spec consistency

- Complete target spec at `specs/inventory-md04-detail-narration/spec.md` describes the realigned description, the new `mrpElementLines` output (core 5 fields per row), fact builder evidence ingestion, narrator guidance extension, frontend projection mirroring, and eval updates. All requirements map to implemented code changes.
- Identifier stability invariant upheld: `capabilityId`, `businessObject`, `bindingId`, `rfcName`, `factTypeRef`, ontology IRIs all unchanged.
- READ-only invariant upheld: `governance.sideEffect: none`, `requiresApproval: false`, no commit/rollback.
- Fact-chain determinism invariant upheld: LLM narrative stays in `narrator.py`; `_SYSTEM_CONSTRAINT` unchanged; no LLM text in `evidence`/`primaryFact`.

# Known limitations and risks

- `mrpElementLines` row field `elementQty` maps SAP field `ELEMENT_QTY`. The repo had no full `MRP_IND_LINES` sample; `ELEMENT_QTY` is the standard MD04 element quantity field, but live SAP confirmation is `not_run` (consistent with the project baseline that live SAP smoke is `not_run`). The executor reads it defensively (null if absent/blank), so a field-name mismatch degrades gracefully to null rather than failing.
- The pre-existing frontend `adapter-integration.test.ts` failure is unrelated and not addressed by this change.
- Contract was updated during Build (brief Scope expanded to include the Java `InventoryAvailabilityExecutor` extraction point, which is the real consumer of `outputMapping`/`MRP_IND_LINES`). This triggered `contract-changed-after-approval` and requires re-confirmation before Verify submission.

# Conclusion

Implementation complete. All change-scoped verification passes: openspec 20/0, agent tests 1139 passed/1 skipped, inventory eval 7/7, Java jco BUILD SUCCESSFUL, frontend 523 passed (1 pre-existing unrelated failure). Awaiting contract re-confirmation to submit Verify.
